title: NetApp StorageGRID Alerts
agents: special-agent(netapp_storagegrid)
catalog: os/storage
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors currently active (unresolved) alerts on a NetApp
 StorageGRID grid, as reported by the Grid Management REST API
 ({GET /api/v3/grid/alerts}).

 A single service is always discovered, since an empty list of alerts
 does not mean there is nothing to monitor.

 The overall service state is derived from the highest severity among
 the currently active alerts (CRITICAL, MAJOR, MINOR). The monitoring
 state used for each severity can be configured via the "NetApp
 StorageGRID alerts" rule set. By default, CRITICAL alerts result in a
 CRIT state, and MAJOR/MINOR alerts result in a WARN state.

 By default, alerts that have been silenced, or that are inhibited by
 another already-counted alert for the same condition, are excluded
 from the state and counts. This can be changed in the rule set.

 The number of alerts per severity is also reported as performance
 data ({netapp_storagegrid_alerts_critical}, {netapp_storagegrid_alerts_major},
 {netapp_storagegrid_alerts_minor}), and up to 20 of the most recent
 alerts are listed in the service details.

item:
 This check does not use an item, only one service per host is created.

discovery:
 One service is created unconditionally.
